rsects l at Y (≠ A). Find XY.\n\nLet me set up coordinates. Let me place B and C on the x-axis.\n\nLet B = (0, 0), C = (14, 0). Then A is such that AB = 15, AC = 13.\n\nA = (x, y) with x² + y² = 225 and (x-14)² + y² = 169.\n\nSubtracting: x² - (x-14)² = 225 - 169 = 56.\nx² - x² + 28x - 196 = 56\n28x = 252\nx = 9.\n\ny² = 225 - 81 = 144, y = 12.\n\nSo A = (9, 12), B = (0, 0), C = (14, 0).\n\nLine l passes through A and is perpendicular to BC. Since BC is along the x-axis, l is vertical: x = 9.\n\nCircumcenter O: equidistant from A, B, C. The circumcenter lies on the perpendicular bisector of BC, which is x = 7.\n\nLet O = (7, k). Then OB² = 49 + k², OA² = (9-7)² + (12-k)² = 4 + (12-k)².\n\nSet equal: 49 + k² = 4 + 144 - 24k + k² = 148 - 24k + k².\n49 = 148 - 24k\n24k = 99\nk = 99/24 = 33/8.\n\nSo O = (7, 33/8).\n\nCircumradius R² = 49 + (33/8)² = 49 + 1089/64 = 3136/64 + 1089/64 = 4225/64. R = 65/8.\n\nCheck: area of triangle with sides 13, 14, 15. s = 21. Area = √(21·8·7·6) = √(7056) = 84. R = abc/(4·Area) = (13·14·15)/(4·84) = 2730/336 = 65/8. ✓\n\nNow, circle through A, B, O. Let me find its equation.\n\nCircle: x² + y² + Dx + Ey + F = 0.\n\nThrough B = (0,0): F = 0.\nThrough A = (9, 12): 81 + 144 + 9D + 12E = 0 → 9D + 12E = -225.\nThrough O = (7, 33/8): 49 + 1089/64 + 7D + (33/8)E = 0.\n49 + 1089/64 = 3136/64 + 1089/64 = 4225/64.\nSo 7D + (33/8)E = -4225/64.\n\nFrom first: D = (-225 - 12E)/9 = -25 - (4/3)E.\n\nSubstitute: 7(-25 - (4/3)E) + (33/8)E = -4225/64.\n-175 - (28/3)E + (33/8)E = -4225/64.\n-(28/3)E + (33/8)E = -4225/64 + 175 = -4225/64 + 11200/64 = 6975/64.\n\n-(28/3) + (33/8) = (-224 + 99)/24 = -125/24.\n\nSo (-125/24)E = 6975/64.\nE = (6975/64) · (-24/125) = -6975·24/(64·125) = -6975·24/8000.\n\n6975/125 = 55.8 = 279/5. So E = -(279/5)·24/64 = -(279/5)·(3/8) = -837/40.\n\nD = -25 - (4/3)(-837/40) = -25 + (4·837)/(3·40) = -25 + 3348/120 = -25 + 279/10 = -250/10 + 279/10 = 29/10.\n\nSo circle 1: x² + y² + (29/10)x - (837/40)y = 0.\n\nLine l: x = 9. Substi