175 = 0.\ny² - (323/24)y + 81 + 175 - 477/2 = 0.\n81 + 175 = 256. 256 - 477/2 = 512/2 - 477/2 = 35/2.\n\ny² - (323/24)y + 35/2 = 0.\n\nOne root is y = 12 (point A). Check: 144 - (323/24)(12) + 35/2 = 144 - 323/2 + 35/2 = 144 - 288/2 = 144 - 144 = 0. ✓\n\nProduct of roots = 35/2. So 12 · y_Y = 35/2 → y_Y = 35/24.\n\nSo Y = (9, 35/24).\n\nXY = |y_X - y_Y| = |357/40 - 35/24|.\n\nCommon denominator: 120.\n357/40 = 1071/120. 35/24 = 175/120.\nXY = (1071 - 175)/120 = 896/120 = 112/15.\n\nCheck if irreducible: gcd(112, 15). 112 = 16·7, 15 = 3·5. gcd = 1. ✓\n\nSo a/b = 112/15, a + b = 127.\n\nLet me verify the computation once more.\n\nX has y = 357/40 = 8.925. Y has y = 35/24 ≈ 1.458. A has y = 12. O has y = 33/8 = 4.125.\n\nX is between A (y=12) and... actually X at y=8.925 is between A and O vertically. Y at y=1.458 is below O. Both on x=9 line.\n\nXY = 8.925 - 1.458 = 7.467 = 112/15 ≈ 7.467. ✓\n\na + b = 112 + 15 = 127.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786705736}
